= Azaña to the Presidency

The Popular Front majority deposes Niceto Alcalá-Zamora - punishing him for the dissolutions of 1935 - and elevates Manuel Azaña to the Presidency of the Republic. It is meant as an honour and a safeguard: the Republic's most capable statesman installed above the fray.

In practice it removes him from the fray. Azaña leaves the premiership for the ceremonial palace of the Pardo, and the government passes to lesser men - Casares Quiroga, able but ailing - just as the crisis deepens. Prieto is blocked from the premiership by his own party's Caballerista wing, so the one figure who might have built a strong government of order is kept out.

[? if coup_progress >= 8 : The generals note, with satisfaction, that the Republic has just weakened its own hand at the worst possible moment. ?] The spring of 1936 slides toward its violent summer with no firm hand on the tiller.
